	"description": "A2: Stoneback, the quarry titan - 17.7 m (58 ft; A3, was 16.8 m / 55 ft) in stone-slab armour (A1's asset), the first signature titan. Breakable plates over weak points (both shoulders, the back, the brow: PlateRules) - a blow on an intact plate keeps 85-90 % from his body and cracks the stone; a broken plate staggers him and leaves a weak point (x2.2 the shoulders, x2.8 the back, x3.0 the brow). A4: his forearm and shin plates break too, and a broken shin (or enough damage to it after) drops him to a knee for six seconds (on_break topple): his shoulders, back and brow come down into a smaller giant's reach and every blow, a Heavy most, lands harder; the lock frames his shins first (lock_bias_m). Phase 1 cycles the trunk smash (a shock line), the sweep (220 degrees: the answer to circling), the boulder and the shoulder charge, which ends against a quarry wall or rock in 3.5 s of reeling. Phase 2 (at 50 % or after three plates broke) opens with his rage and chains faster: the raging smash runs into the raging sweep. Tuned to kill a stage-3 or 4 giant in a few blows, to fall to a stage-5 giant who topples him in a hard fight and to a stage-6 giant in about three minutes (docs/BALANCE_LOG.md, A2-A4).",
